1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,540
You're here.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,380
Your organs are failing.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,300
And your death is drawing near.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,440
But if you bribe the right politicians in the right order at the right time,

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,600
you can trade the nuclear warheads for medicine.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,080
And it's not even a crime.

7
00:01:40,524 --> 00:01:41,324
N.I.H.

8
00:01:41,324 --> 00:01:46,384
Fails to Institute Health A root cause failure analysis to show why the

9
00:01:46,924 --> 00:01:51,604
world's largest medical research institution only allocates three point

10
00:01:51,604 --> 00:01:56,264
three percent of its budget to testing which of the thousands of known-safe

11
00:01:56,384 --> 00:01:58,644
treatments actually work in humans.

12
00:01:59,624 --> 00:02:04,244
Oxford tested COVID treatments for five hundred dollars per patient and

13
00:02:04,244 --> 00:02:07,244
saved a million lives in one hundred days.

14
00:02:08,204 --> 00:02:09,264
The N.I.H.

15
00:02:09,284 --> 00:02:15,224
spent one point six billion dollars and completed zero trials in four years.

16
00:02:15,944 --> 00:02:17,694
A Tale of Two Trials.

17
00:02:18,424 --> 00:02:23,364
The difference between efficient and inefficient trial design isn't theoretical.

18
00:02:23,964 --> 00:02:28,724
Your species accidentally ran a controlled experiment on itself during COVID.

19
00:02:29,424 --> 00:02:30,124
Two countries.

20
00:02:30,644 --> 00:02:31,284
Same disease.

21
00:02:31,704 --> 00:02:34,124
One spent like it was trying to cure death.

22
00:02:34,644 --> 00:02:36,184
The other actually did.

23
00:02:36,804 --> 00:02:38,724
RECOVERY Trial (U.K.

24
00:02:38,724 --> 00:02:39,224
Approach).

25
00:02:39,784 --> 00:02:43,104
The British spent twenty million dollars over six months.

26
00:02:43,684 --> 00:02:45,984
Enrolled forty-eight thousand patients.

27
00:02:46,484 --> 00:02:50,764
Found multiple effective treatments, including dexamethasone, a steroid

28
00:02:50,764 --> 00:02:53,554
that had been available since nineteen fifty-seven.

29
00:02:54,624 --> 00:03:00,124
It reduced COVID deaths by one-third and saved over one million lives.

30
00:03:00,984 --> 00:03:01,744
Cost per patient:

31
00:03:02,444 --> 00:03:03,684
five hundred dollars.

32
00:03:04,624 --> 00:03:06,524
RECOVER Initiative (N.I.H.

33
00:03:06,684 --> 00:03:07,184
Approach).

34
00:03:08,024 --> 00:03:12,064
Nearly six hundred potential treatments for Long COVID have been identified.

35
00:03:12,664 --> 00:03:17,304
At RECOVERY trial efficiency (five hundred dollars per patient, five thousand

36
00:03:17,304 --> 00:03:19,004
five hundred patients per treatment),

37
00:03:19,864 --> 00:03:25,024
one point six six five billion dollars buys six hundred completed trials.

38
00:03:25,864 --> 00:03:26,924
The N.I.H.

39
00:03:27,064 --> 00:03:29,804
received one point six six five billion dollars.

40
00:03:30,284 --> 00:03:33,424
Over four years, they completed zero.

41
00:03:34,624 --> 00:03:38,164
Only fifteen percent of the budget went to clinical trials;

42
00:03:38,164 --> 00:03:42,564
the rest funded observational studies, data management, and administration.

43
00:03:43,284 --> 00:03:48,023
Of those enrolled, roughly eleven percent were in interventional trials

44
00:03:48,023 --> 00:03:49,683
that actually tested treatments.

45
00:03:50,623 --> 00:03:54,704
The other eighty-nine percent were in observational studies, which is the

46
00:03:54,704 --> 00:03:57,264
medical equivalent of taking attendance at a funeral.

47
00:03:58,424 --> 00:04:00,264
Cost per interventional patient:

48
00:04:01,084 --> 00:04:06,014
five hundred and four thousand, five hundred dollars, the price of a house.

49
00:04:06,584 --> 00:04:08,844
Nobody got a house and nobody got cured.

50
00:04:09,804 --> 00:04:10,434
They got observed.

51
00:04:11,384 --> 00:04:12,484
Expensively.

52
00:04:12,524 --> 00:04:14,184
The observation was very thorough.

53
00:04:14,744 --> 00:04:15,624
It has been peer-reviewed.

54
00:04:16,284 --> 00:04:18,304
The peers also observed the patients.

55
00:04:18,904 --> 00:04:22,294
The patients are still sick, but they are the most well-documented

56
00:04:22,904 --> 00:04:25,824
sick people in the history of sickness.

57
00:04:26,524 --> 00:04:27,184
It gets worse.

58
00:04:27,884 --> 00:04:32,684
The treatments RECOVER eventually selected were called "truly absurd" by

59
00:04:32,684 --> 00:04:34,144
patient advocates.

60
00:04:34,304 --> 00:04:39,174
Low-dose naltrexone, the number one patient-requested treatment (generic,

61
00:04:39,624 --> 00:04:44,604
cheap, already showing results in independent studies), was excluded for

62
00:04:44,604 --> 00:04:48,744
over two years before finally being added in round two.

63
00:04:49,564 --> 00:04:53,664
David Putrino, director of rehabilitation innovation at Mount Sinai, called

64
00:04:53,664 --> 00:04:55,924
the spending "largely wasted".

65
00:04:56,744 --> 00:04:59,644
Researchers outside RECOVER had lists of drugs to test.

66
00:05:00,244 --> 00:05:01,444
The system ignored them.

67
00:05:02,704 --> 00:05:05,514
Six hundred trials were possible with that money.

68
00:05:06,064 --> 00:05:07,184
Zero were completed.

69
00:05:07,924 --> 00:05:11,864
That is the difference between a system that tests treatments and a system

70
00:05:11,864 --> 00:05:13,414
that tests patience.

71
00:05:14,444 --> 00:05:16,504
The Translation Crisis:

72
00:05:16,564 --> 00:05:19,384
All Theory, No Medicine.

73
00:05:19,444 --> 00:05:21,524
Basic research is not the problem.

74
00:05:22,224 --> 00:05:26,444
Five decades of N.I.H.-funded science built one of the largest drug candidate

75
00:05:26,444 --> 00:05:28,244
pipelines in history.

76
00:05:28,524 --> 00:05:30,024
Researchers identified targets,

77
00:05:30,884 --> 00:05:33,664
characterized molecules, established safety profiles.

78
00:05:34,064 --> 00:05:36,694
That work was essential, and it succeeded.

79
00:05:37,624 --> 00:05:40,924
The problem is what happens after the discoveries are made:

80
00:05:41,744 --> 00:05:42,324
almost nothing.

81
00:05:43,104 --> 00:05:44,204
The pipeline is full.

82
00:05:44,524 --> 00:05:45,644
The exit is closed.

83
00:05:46,624 --> 00:05:50,804
COVID made this visible for the first time, but it is the institution's

84
00:05:50,804 --> 00:05:52,204
default setting;

85
00:05:52,244 --> 00:05:55,614
the way you don't notice a leaking roof until it rains inside.

86
00:05:56,224 --> 00:05:59,404
It has been raining inside for fifty years.

87
00:06:00,024 --> 00:06:00,823
The N.I.H.

88
00:06:00,823 --> 00:06:03,544
has published several papers on indoor rain.

89
00:06:04,064 --> 00:06:07,644
There are over twenty thousand F.D.A.-approved drugs that are known to be

90
00:06:07,644 --> 00:06:08,514
safe in humans.

91
00:06:09,084 --> 00:06:11,804
Thousands more clinically-tested candidates are gathering dust,

92
00:06:12,424 --> 00:06:15,684
including over three thousand marketed drugs that could be repurposed for

93
00:06:15,684 --> 00:06:17,504
diseases nobody's tried them on.

94
00:06:18,344 --> 00:06:21,844
In Alzheimer's alone, researchers have identified hundreds of safe drugs

95
00:06:21,844 --> 00:06:25,724
worth testing, yet less than ten percent are in active trials.

96
00:06:26,264 --> 00:06:29,404
And the number of clinical trials available for your grandma in St.

97
00:06:29,544 --> 00:06:30,044
Louis?

98
00:06:30,284 --> 00:06:30,784
Zero.

99
00:06:31,444 --> 00:06:35,104
You have a warehouse of safe molecules that have never been systematically

100
00:06:35,104 --> 00:06:36,644
tested for new uses.

101
00:06:37,024 --> 00:06:38,064
The warehouse is full.

102
00:06:38,424 --> 00:06:41,244
The testing facility is closed for a team-building retreat.

103
00:06:42,164 --> 00:06:42,954
This is not hypothetical.

104
00:06:43,704 --> 00:06:47,664
In twenty twenty-three, researchers published case reports of severe long

105
00:06:47,664 --> 00:06:52,004
COVID patients experiencing complete remission within days of receiving

106
00:06:52,004 --> 00:06:53,944
monoclonal antibody infusions.

107
00:06:54,724 --> 00:06:58,924
Previously bedridden patients returned to normal lives, with remissions

108
00:06:58,924 --> 00:07:00,744
sustained over two years.

109
00:07:01,384 --> 00:07:02,124
The U.S.

110
00:07:02,124 --> 00:07:05,784
government had spent over five billion dollars purchasing millions of doses

111
00:07:05,784 --> 00:07:08,184
of these same antibodies for acute COVID.

112
00:07:09,164 --> 00:07:13,004
When Omicron rendered them ineffective for acute treatment, millions of

113
00:07:13,084 --> 00:07:15,644
unused doses sat in refrigerated storage.

114
00:07:16,324 --> 00:07:20,164
Long COVID patients, having read the case reports, begged for access.

115
00:07:20,764 --> 00:07:22,004
They organized petitions.

116
00:07:22,464 --> 00:07:23,524
They cited the remissions.

117
00:07:24,004 --> 00:07:25,124
The government said no.

118
00:07:25,504 --> 00:07:29,684
The doses were authorized for acute COVID only, and the authorization had

119
00:07:29,684 --> 00:07:33,604
been revoked because they didn't work for acute COVID, which meant they

120
00:07:33,604 --> 00:07:36,484
could not be given to anyone, for anything, ever.

121
00:07:37,384 --> 00:07:39,964
The antibodies matched the original variants;

122
00:07:40,024 --> 00:07:43,284
the long COVID patients had been infected by the original variants.

123
00:07:43,884 --> 00:07:45,244
Nobody tested this.

124
00:07:45,344 --> 00:07:46,544
Nobody ran trials.

125
00:07:46,944 --> 00:07:49,084
Nobody repurposed the stockpile.

126
00:07:49,764 --> 00:07:54,204
The first formal Phase two trial of monoclonal antibodies for long COVID

127
00:07:54,204 --> 00:07:56,684
is scheduled for mid-twenty twenty-six,

128
00:07:57,484 --> 00:08:01,924
four years after the doses were available and several years after they expired.

129
00:08:02,584 --> 00:08:04,924
Five billion dollars of medicine.

130
00:08:05,024 --> 00:08:06,044
Millions of doses.

131
00:08:06,444 --> 00:08:07,864
Patients who wanted them.

132
00:08:08,324 --> 00:08:10,004
Case reports showing they worked.

133
00:08:10,604 --> 00:08:11,934
The doses expired.

134
00:08:12,284 --> 00:08:13,604
The patients didn't;

135
00:08:13,684 --> 00:08:15,184
they just kept being sick.

136
00:08:15,904 --> 00:08:19,704
Your government threw away the cure and kept the disease.

137
00:08:20,584 --> 00:08:24,564
On Wishonia, we have a word for this, but it is a word I am not permitted

138
00:08:24,564 --> 00:08:29,124
to use in your language because it is considered a slur against the competence

139
00:08:29,124 --> 00:08:33,764
of your entire species, so I will simply note that the word exists and move

140
00:08:33,764 --> 00:08:34,264
on.

141
00:08:35,184 --> 00:08:36,804
Then there's metformin.

142
00:08:36,864 --> 00:08:40,424
A phase three randomized controlled trial, or R.C.T.

143
00:08:40,664 --> 00:08:45,224
(COVID-OUT) showed it reduces long COVID incidence by forty-one percent.

144
00:08:45,704 --> 00:08:47,804
It costs four dollars a month.

145
00:08:48,404 --> 00:08:50,154
It has been generic for decades.

146
00:08:50,324 --> 00:08:51,624
It is globally available.

147
00:08:52,224 --> 00:08:52,964
The N.I.H.

148
00:08:53,044 --> 00:08:54,244
guideline response:

149
00:08:54,244 --> 00:08:57,024
"insufficient evidence to recommend for or against".

150
00:08:57,944 --> 00:09:02,044
Long COVID costs one hundred and seventy billion dollars a year.

151
00:09:02,644 --> 00:09:07,424
The four dollar pill that cuts it by forty-one percent has no corporate

152
00:09:07,424 --> 00:09:10,644
sponsor, because nobody profits from a generic.

153
00:09:11,144 --> 00:09:14,344
This is the entire chapter in one sentence.

154
00:09:14,544 --> 00:09:16,424
To appreciate the scale:

155
00:09:16,584 --> 00:09:18,444
long COVID costs the U.S.

156
00:09:18,464 --> 00:09:23,344
an estimated one hundred and seventy billion dollars annually in lost wages

157
00:09:23,344 --> 00:09:27,804
alone, with roughly seventeen million Americans currently affected.

158
00:09:28,524 --> 00:09:32,924
A RECOVERY-style pragmatic trial would have cost approximately twenty-four

159
00:09:32,924 --> 00:09:35,804
million dollars and could have produced results in months.

160
00:09:36,484 --> 00:09:40,524
Instead, your government spent five billion dollars buying the medicine

161
00:09:40,524 --> 00:09:45,244
and is now paying one hundred and seventy billion dollars a year in economic

162
00:09:45,244 --> 00:09:48,244
damage from the disease it didn't bother to treat.

163
00:09:49,004 --> 00:09:52,724
The ratio of what you're losing to what the trial would have cost is seven

164
00:09:52,724 --> 00:09:54,784
thousand and eighty-three to one.

165
00:09:55,624 --> 00:09:56,604
The N.I.H.

166
00:09:56,764 --> 00:10:00,644
is, by its own metrics, a publishing house that occasionally dabbles in

167
00:10:00,644 --> 00:10:01,224
medicine.

168
00:10:01,664 --> 00:10:05,704
It publishes two point five million funded papers annually.

169
00:10:06,104 --> 00:10:09,844
It produces approximately fifty new drug approvals annually.

170
00:10:10,204 --> 00:10:14,804
That's a conversion rate from paper to patient of zero point zero zero two

171
00:10:14,804 --> 00:10:15,403
percent.

172
00:10:16,364 --> 00:10:18,464
For every fifty thousand papers,

173
00:10:19,124 --> 00:10:20,663
one drug reaches a human.

174
00:10:21,184 --> 00:10:25,124
The rest become citations in other papers, which become citations in other

175
00:10:25,124 --> 00:10:29,364
papers, in an infinite loop of academics reading each other's homework.

176
00:10:30,064 --> 00:10:32,994
On Wishonia, we call this a "knowledge ouroboros."

177
00:10:33,704 --> 00:10:35,604
It looks productive from the inside.

178
00:10:35,904 --> 00:10:39,764
From the outside, it's a snake eating its own tail and writing a paper about

179
00:10:39,764 --> 00:10:40,744
the nutritional content.

180
00:10:41,644 --> 00:10:42,574
Plenty of Knowledge.

181
00:10:43,024 --> 00:10:43,884
No Translation.

182
00:10:44,864 --> 00:10:48,264
About five percent of patients have participated in clinical trials.

183
00:10:48,724 --> 00:10:52,684
About forty-four point eight percent would participate if invited.

184
00:10:53,224 --> 00:10:57,184
About nine to eleven percent have ever been invited.

185
00:10:57,384 --> 00:11:00,464
Nearly half of all patients would join a trial if asked.

186
00:11:01,084 --> 00:11:02,444
Almost nobody asks.

187
00:11:03,084 --> 00:11:07,124
Your species has a room full of volunteers holding their hands up, and a

188
00:11:07,124 --> 00:11:09,884
system that looked at the room and decided to study the

189
00:11:10,644 --> 00:11:11,364
clipboard instead.

190
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:14,004
The clipboard is very well-studied.

191
00:11:14,384 --> 00:11:15,754
It has been studied for decades.

192
00:11:16,204 --> 00:11:18,514
Multiple papers have been written about the clipboard.

193
00:11:18,964 --> 00:11:20,074
One of them won an award.

194
00:11:20,804 --> 00:11:22,984
The volunteers are still holding their hands up.

195
00:11:23,464 --> 00:11:24,644
Some of them have died.

196
00:11:25,104 --> 00:11:26,544
This has been noted on the clipboard.

197
00:11:27,384 --> 00:11:31,984
Understanding disease and testing treatments in humans are completely different

198
00:11:31,984 --> 00:11:32,804
activities.

199
00:11:33,264 --> 00:11:34,664
One requires microscopes.

200
00:11:35,124 --> 00:11:39,054
The other requires giving people medicine and seeing if they stop dying.

201
00:11:39,444 --> 00:11:43,464
In nineteen seventy, spending heavily on microscopes made sense;

202
00:11:43,504 --> 00:11:45,214
you didn't know enough to test intelligently.

203
00:11:46,004 --> 00:11:50,744
In twenty twenty-five, after two point five million papers a year for five

204
00:11:50,744 --> 00:11:53,104
decades, the ratio should have shifted.

205
00:11:53,764 --> 00:11:54,264
It didn't.

206
00:11:54,924 --> 00:11:55,824
The N.I.H.

207
00:11:55,824 --> 00:11:56,324
chose

208
00:11:56,444 --> 00:12:00,224
microscopes in nineteen seventy and has not reconsidered since, which is

209
00:12:00,224 --> 00:12:04,124
the institutional equivalent of still crawling because you learned to crawl

210
00:12:04,124 --> 00:12:05,344
before you learned to walk.

211
00:12:06,164 --> 00:12:08,284
The Allocation Problem.

212
00:12:08,324 --> 00:12:12,484
Your National Institutes of Health has the word "Health" in its name and

213
00:12:12,484 --> 00:12:15,724
an annual budget of forty-seven billion dollars.

214
00:12:16,364 --> 00:12:19,724
Fifty-five million of you die annually from disease.

215
00:12:20,204 --> 00:12:22,724
You would think those two facts would be related.

216
00:12:23,284 --> 00:12:23,784
They are not.

217
00:12:24,104 --> 00:12:27,244
Of two hundred and forty-seven billion dollars the N.I.H.

218
00:12:27,364 --> 00:12:31,804
spent over a decade, exactly three point three percent went to testing which

219
00:12:31,804 --> 00:12:35,344
of the thousands of known-safe treatments actually work in humans.

220
00:12:36,104 --> 00:12:40,664
The other ninety-six point seven percent funded understanding disease mechanisms,

221
00:12:40,764 --> 00:12:46,024
translating discoveries toward (but never into) clinical use, training scientists,

222
00:12:46,344 --> 00:12:49,884
observational programs that spend billions watching disease without treating

223
00:12:49,884 --> 00:12:54,544
it, and a side quest engineering bat viruses, which is called "research"

224
00:12:54,664 --> 00:12:57,714
the way watching someone drown from a boat is called "lifeguarding.".

225
00:12:59,204 --> 00:13:01,064
Basic research is not the problem.

226
00:13:01,784 --> 00:13:04,304
Understanding disease is how you find candidates to test.

227
00:13:05,004 --> 00:13:08,904
The problem is that after fifty years and a trillion dollars, the ratio

228
00:13:08,904 --> 00:13:09,844
hasn't moved.

229
00:13:10,684 --> 00:13:14,924
The marginal value of the eighty-fifth cent on basic research is near zero

230
00:13:14,924 --> 00:13:18,884
when you're spending three cents on the only activity that turns research

231
00:13:18,884 --> 00:13:19,944
into medicine.

232
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:21,834
You don't have a knowledge deficit.

233
00:13:22,464 --> 00:13:23,974
You have an allocation deficit.

234
00:13:25,344 --> 00:13:29,164
Three point three percent on trials might be defensible if the testing queue

235
00:13:29,164 --> 00:13:29,664
were empty.

236
00:13:30,344 --> 00:13:30,864
It isn't.

237
00:13:31,444 --> 00:13:34,944
There are roughly nine thousand five hundred compounds with established

238
00:13:34,944 --> 00:13:39,544
safety profiles, and ninety-nine point seven percent of their possible disease

239
00:13:39,544 --> 00:13:42,204
applications have never been tested.

240
00:13:42,464 --> 00:13:46,784
Most are off-patent, which means no pharmaceutical company will fund trials

241
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:49,364
for them, which means the N.I.H.

242
00:13:49,364 --> 00:13:54,204
is the only entity that could, which means it is specifically choosing not

243
00:13:54,204 --> 00:13:56,684
to do the one thing only it can do.

244
00:13:57,284 --> 00:13:59,204
The pipeline is overflowing with candidates.

245
00:13:59,924 --> 00:14:01,444
The bottleneck is trials.

246
00:14:01,964 --> 00:14:03,564
The drugs are sitting there.

247
00:14:03,724 --> 00:14:04,224
Safe.

248
00:14:04,544 --> 00:14:05,264
Ready.

249
00:14:05,264 --> 00:14:06,304
Unpatentable.

250
00:14:06,884 --> 00:14:08,154
They've been waiting for decades.

251
00:14:08,784 --> 00:14:11,684
Some of them have been waiting longer than most of your scientists have

252
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:12,384
been alive.

253
00:14:13,064 --> 00:14:16,844
It's like spending ninety-six point seven percent of your grocery budget

254
00:14:16,844 --> 00:14:21,544
on cookbooks and three point three percent on food, then wondering why you're

255
00:14:21,544 --> 00:14:22,064
starving.

256
00:14:22,544 --> 00:14:26,484
Except the cookbooks are very prestigious and the starving people aren't

257
00:14:26,484 --> 00:14:29,184
on the committee that decides whether to buy more cookbooks.

258
00:14:29,904 --> 00:14:30,624
A J.A.M.A.

259
00:14:30,624 --> 00:14:34,124
study broke down two hundred and forty-seven point three billion dollars

260
00:14:34,124 --> 00:14:34,904
in N.I.H.

261
00:14:35,024 --> 00:14:37,364
spending (twenty ten to twenty nineteen).

262
00:14:38,084 --> 00:14:42,284
I have organized it from "largest amount spent not on clinical trials" to

263
00:14:42,784 --> 00:14:44,824
"smallest amount spent not clinical trials,"

264
00:14:45,484 --> 00:14:48,924
though I should note that none of it is labeled "not clinical trials."

265
00:14:49,264 --> 00:14:51,424
It is labeled "investment in the future."

266
00:14:52,084 --> 00:14:55,124
The future has been invested in for fifty years.

267
00:14:55,684 --> 00:14:56,944
It has not yet arrived.

268
00:14:57,544 --> 00:15:01,084
Eighty-four point nine percent, or two hundred and nine point nine billion

269
00:15:01,084 --> 00:15:05,344
dollars, is dedicated to basic research for understanding disease mechanisms,

270
00:15:06,404 --> 00:15:08,464
molecular biology, and genomics;

271
00:15:08,564 --> 00:15:12,764
while essential for identifying new targets, eighty-five cents of every

272
00:15:12,764 --> 00:15:15,984
dollar is a lot of understanding and not much testing.

273
00:15:16,984 --> 00:15:20,524
Eleven point eight percent, or twenty-nine point three billion dollars,

274
00:15:20,984 --> 00:15:26,204
goes to non-trial applied research that translates discoveries toward practical

275
00:15:26,204 --> 00:15:30,064
use, but without the final step of testing them in patients.

276
00:15:31,004 --> 00:15:35,844
The Clinical and Translational Science Awards, or C.T.S.A., infrastructure

277
00:15:35,844 --> 00:15:40,734
program spends about one billion dollars per year in trial infrastructure,

278
00:15:41,364 --> 00:15:43,504
coordination, and training.

279
00:15:43,744 --> 00:15:48,484
Observational studies for population health data collection (such as large-scale

280
00:15:48,484 --> 00:15:53,664
observational cohorts costing two point one six billion dollars) are valuable

281
00:15:53,664 --> 00:15:58,524
for identifying patterns, but observation without intervention doesn't cure

282
00:15:58,524 --> 00:15:59,024
anyone.

283
00:15:59,864 --> 00:16:04,664
Other applied research includes drug characterization, health services research,

284
00:16:04,664 --> 00:16:05,784
and epidemiology.

285
00:16:06,544 --> 00:16:11,804
Only three point three percent, or eight point one billion dollars, is spent

286
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:16,444
on phased clinical trials, which is the only category that directly tests

287
00:16:16,684 --> 00:16:20,184
whether treatments work in humans through phases one to three.

288
00:16:21,204 --> 00:16:25,104
Phase one accounts for one point five billion dollars, or eighteen point

289
00:16:25,104 --> 00:16:27,264
five percent of the clinical trial budget.

290
00:16:27,804 --> 00:16:31,484
Phase two accounts for three point five billion dollars, or forty-three

291
00:16:31,484 --> 00:16:32,424
point two percent.

292
00:16:33,164 --> 00:16:37,584
Phase three accounts for two point six billion dollars, or thirty-two point

293
00:16:37,584 --> 00:16:38,244
one percent.

294
00:16:39,084 --> 00:16:39,764
The N.I.H.

295
00:16:40,064 --> 00:16:44,584
covers only three point seven to four point three percent of Phase three

296
00:16:44,584 --> 00:16:45,084
costs,

297
00:16:45,844 --> 00:16:47,124
leaving completion to industry,

298
00:16:47,744 --> 00:16:50,784
which only funds trials with patent-protected profit potential.

299
00:16:51,984 --> 00:16:56,884
Other unclassified spending totals zero point five billion dollars, or six

300
00:16:56,884 --> 00:16:57,684
point two percent,

301
00:16:58,504 --> 00:17:02,784
for cross-phase overhead, pilot studies, and trials not classified to a

302
00:17:02,784 --> 00:17:03,464
single phase.

303
00:17:04,324 --> 00:17:10,004
Pragmatic trials (eighty-two times cheaper per patient) are severely underfunded

304
00:17:10,004 --> 00:17:11,784
despite proven efficiency.

305
00:17:12,904 --> 00:17:14,544
Why This Allocation Exists.

306
00:17:15,004 --> 00:17:17,074
This is not the fault of individual researchers.

307
00:17:17,964 --> 00:17:20,824
Most became scientists because they wanted to cure diseases.

308
00:17:21,424 --> 00:17:26,204
The system they work in rewards everything except curing diseases, and those

309
00:17:26,204 --> 00:17:29,034
rewards were designed by someone else entirely.

310
00:17:30,024 --> 00:17:34,204
Huge drug companies with political influence love the N.I.H.

311
00:17:34,344 --> 00:17:36,964
Taxpayers absorb the risk of basic research;

312
00:17:36,984 --> 00:17:38,544
industry patents whatever works.

313
00:17:39,064 --> 00:17:42,584
It's like if your neighbor paid for your kitchen renovation, and then you

314
00:17:42,644 --> 00:17:44,504
charged them rent to eat there.

315
00:17:45,344 --> 00:17:48,184
But independent trials comparing drugs head-to-head?

316
00:17:48,764 --> 00:17:50,164
Those are terrifying.

317
00:17:50,704 --> 00:17:54,524
They might reveal that the eighty thousand dollar drug works about as well

318
00:17:54,524 --> 00:17:56,044
as the four dollar generic.

319
00:17:56,764 --> 00:18:01,484
PhRMA, the pharmaceutical lobby, has consistently opposed comparative effectiveness

320
00:18:01,484 --> 00:18:02,164
research.

321
00:18:02,844 --> 00:18:05,024
When Congress created P.C.O.R.I.

322
00:18:05,264 --> 00:18:10,244
(the Patient-Centered Outcomes Research Institute) in twenty-ten, industry

323
00:18:10,244 --> 00:18:15,184
successfully lobbied to prohibit it from making coverage recommendations

324
00:18:15,184 --> 00:18:16,424
based on cost-effectiveness.

325
00:18:17,824 --> 00:18:22,784
Congress literally passed a law saying "don't fund research that might lower

326
00:18:22,784 --> 00:18:23,504
drug prices."

327
00:18:24,184 --> 00:18:25,444
They wrote it down.

328
00:18:25,804 --> 00:18:26,744
In legislation.

329
00:18:27,384 --> 00:18:28,044
On purpose.

330
00:18:28,704 --> 00:18:29,744
With their names on it.

331
00:18:30,324 --> 00:18:33,884
And then they went home and told their constituents they were fighting for

332
00:18:33,884 --> 00:18:38,664
affordable healthcare, because your species' capacity for doublethink is

333
00:18:38,664 --> 00:18:40,684
genuinely Olympian.

334
00:18:41,044 --> 00:18:44,644
This pattern held during the deadliest pandemic in a century.

335
00:18:45,323 --> 00:18:49,464
Operation Warp Speed initially selected fourteen vaccine candidates and

336
00:18:49,464 --> 00:18:52,323
planned head-to-head comparative studies in primates.

337
00:18:52,843 --> 00:18:56,073
Then dropped the comparative studies without explanation.

338
00:18:56,563 --> 00:19:00,083
Backed five companies with billions, gave others nothing.

339
00:19:00,784 --> 00:19:04,323
The selection process was opaque enough to draw Senate scrutiny;

340
00:19:04,424 --> 00:19:08,864
when Senator Tammy Baldwin asked the Biomedical Advanced Research and Development

341
00:19:08,864 --> 00:19:13,324
Authority, or BARDA's acting director to name the companies receiving public

342
00:19:13,324 --> 00:19:17,924
funds, he refused, citing "procurement sensitivity".

343
00:19:18,044 --> 00:19:21,464
No published cost-benefit analysis for excluding any candidate.

344
00:19:22,324 --> 00:19:23,584
The W.H.O.

345
00:19:23,584 --> 00:19:28,484
ran a Solidarity Trial for Vaccines doing exactly this kind of head-to-head

346
00:19:28,484 --> 00:19:29,324
comparison.

347
00:19:29,784 --> 00:19:30,384
The U.S.

348
00:19:30,624 --> 00:19:31,324
didn't join.

349
00:19:31,924 --> 00:19:32,824
Notice the pattern:

350
00:19:33,284 --> 00:19:38,524
the Patient-Centered Outcomes Research Institute, or PCORI is banned from

351
00:19:38,524 --> 00:19:40,444
comparing drug cost-effectiveness.

352
00:19:41,024 --> 00:19:46,064
Researching COVID to Enhance Recovery, or RECOVER ignores the treatments

353
00:19:46,064 --> 00:19:47,604
patients actually want.

354
00:19:48,804 --> 00:19:49,604
O.W.S.

355
00:19:49,664 --> 00:19:50,824
drops the comparative monkey studies.

356
00:19:51,764 --> 00:19:54,764
Every manufacturer has financial interests;

357
00:19:54,944 --> 00:19:58,584
Pfizer had them, Moderna had them, and that wasn't disqualifying.

358
00:19:59,224 --> 00:20:03,264
"Financial interest" only becomes a reason not to test when the treatment

359
00:20:03,384 --> 00:20:03,964
is cheap,

360
00:20:04,564 --> 00:20:06,864
generic, or threatens incumbent revenue.

361
00:20:07,084 --> 00:20:11,104
The system tests what's profitable and ignores what isn't.

362
00:20:11,344 --> 00:20:13,224
The revolving door helps.

363
00:20:13,244 --> 00:20:13,884
N.I.H.

364
00:20:13,984 --> 00:20:16,144
advisory committees include industry representatives.

365
00:20:16,784 --> 00:20:17,784
Former N.I.H.

366
00:20:17,784 --> 00:20:19,444
officials join pharmaceutical boards.

367
00:20:20,084 --> 00:20:22,764
Academic researchers depend on industry grants.

368
00:20:23,424 --> 00:20:28,224
Everyone's incentives align against cheap, fast trials testing whether expensive

369
00:20:28,224 --> 00:20:30,364
drugs outperform generics.

370
00:20:31,104 --> 00:20:32,284
It's not a conspiracy.

371
00:20:33,024 --> 00:20:34,684
Conspiracies require secrecy.

372
00:20:35,124 --> 00:20:35,754
This is all public.

373
00:20:36,264 --> 00:20:40,204
It's just that everyone involved happens to benefit from the same terrible

374
00:20:40,204 --> 00:20:40,904
outcome,

375
00:20:41,684 --> 00:20:44,524
purely by coincidence, repeatedly, for decades.

376
00:20:45,144 --> 00:20:47,204
On Wishonia, we have a word for this.

377
00:20:47,924 --> 00:20:49,764
The word is "conspiracy."

378
00:20:50,064 --> 00:20:53,664
The difference between a conspiracy and a system is whether the participants

379
00:20:53,684 --> 00:20:55,364
need to meet in a dark room.

380
00:20:55,844 --> 00:20:58,124
These people meet in conference rooms with catering.

381
00:20:58,484 --> 00:21:00,244
The outcome is identical.

382
00:21:00,504 --> 00:21:03,904
The three point three percent allocation isn't a mystery.

383
00:21:03,964 --> 00:21:04,764
It's a business model.

384
00:21:05,524 --> 00:21:07,424
Basic research produces publications.

385
00:21:07,704 --> 00:21:09,204
Publications produce tenure.

386
00:21:09,564 --> 00:21:10,924
Tenure produces more grants.

387
00:21:11,604 --> 00:21:14,024
Individual researchers want cures.

388
00:21:14,064 --> 00:21:17,744
The system rewards them for everything except producing one.

389
00:21:18,244 --> 00:21:22,564
Actual treatments are a byproduct that occasionally happens when someone

390
00:21:22,564 --> 00:21:27,724
forgets to optimize for papers and accidentally optimizes for results instead.

391
00:21:28,344 --> 00:21:32,004
It's like a restaurant where the chefs are passionate about food but get

392
00:21:32,004 --> 00:21:34,934
promoted based on how many menus they print.

393
00:21:35,144 --> 00:21:36,824
The menus are exquisite.

394
00:21:36,904 --> 00:21:37,694
They have won awards.

395
00:21:38,404 --> 00:21:39,964
The diners are eating the menus.

396
00:21:40,744 --> 00:21:42,264
Nobody has mentioned this.

397
00:21:42,644 --> 00:21:44,294
You Pay Twice.

398
00:21:44,524 --> 00:21:45,584
The N.I.H.

399
00:21:45,584 --> 00:21:48,924
claims to produce "public goods" like open science and training.

400
00:21:49,344 --> 00:21:52,224
What it actually produces is a free R. and D.

401
00:21:52,224 --> 00:21:56,004
department for pharmaceutical companies, funded by the same people who then

402
00:21:56,004 --> 00:21:57,784
pay full price for the drugs.

403
00:21:58,464 --> 00:22:03,664
Taxpayers funded research behind ninety-nine percent of new drugs (three

404
00:22:03,664 --> 00:22:07,064
hundred and fifty-six drugs, twenty-ten to twenty-nineteen).

405
00:22:08,024 --> 00:22:09,784
Industry patents the winners.

406
00:22:10,324 --> 00:22:13,124
The public pays again through high drug prices.

407
00:22:13,744 --> 00:22:17,044
When research leads to a dead end, the public eats the loss.

408
00:22:17,624 --> 00:22:19,074
You pay for the lottery ticket.

409
00:22:19,524 --> 00:22:20,484
They cash the winnings.

410
00:22:21,164 --> 00:22:24,484
You'd think someone would have mentioned this arrangement before now, and

411
00:22:24,484 --> 00:22:29,624
someone has, many times, but the people who cash the winnings also fund

412
00:22:29,624 --> 00:22:34,064
the campaigns of the people who could change the arrangement, so the arrangement

413
00:22:34,064 --> 00:22:34,644
continues.

414
00:22:35,584 --> 00:22:37,544
The only things the N.I.H.

415
00:22:37,544 --> 00:22:41,764
*should* fund are things private companies *cannot* profitably fund:

416
00:22:42,524 --> 00:22:47,464
open pragmatic trial platforms, repurposing of generic drugs where no patent

417
00:22:47,464 --> 00:22:49,364
means no profit means no interest,

418
00:22:50,124 --> 00:22:54,944
and comparative effectiveness data from head-to-head trials revealing which

419
00:22:54,944 --> 00:23:00,164
drugs actually work best (pharma's nightmare, your potential salvation).

420
00:23:00,744 --> 00:23:02,484
Instead, the N.I.H.

421
00:23:02,904 --> 00:23:06,004
explicitly avoids them to "not crowd out industry."

422
00:23:06,364 --> 00:23:06,964
Translation:

423
00:23:07,404 --> 00:23:10,944
"We won't run the trials that would lower drug prices, because the people

424
00:23:10,944 --> 00:23:13,584
who set drug prices asked us nicely."

425
00:23:14,144 --> 00:23:17,704
They asked nicely and also spent one hundred and twenty-seven million dollars

426
00:23:17,704 --> 00:23:20,144
on lobbying, but the niceness was noted.

427
00:23:20,664 --> 00:23:22,604
The Patient Disconnect:

428
00:23:22,844 --> 00:23:24,944
Zero Correlation with Health Outcomes.

429
00:23:25,424 --> 00:23:27,284
Correlation between N.I.H.

430
00:23:27,364 --> 00:23:29,764
funding priorities and actual disease burden:

431
00:23:30,644 --> 00:23:32,744
zero point zero seven.

432
00:23:33,564 --> 00:23:34,444
That is not a typo.

433
00:23:34,844 --> 00:23:39,844
On a scale of zero (random) to one (perfect), the N.I.H.

434
00:23:39,844 --> 00:23:41,404
scores "basically a coin flip."

435
00:23:42,144 --> 00:23:45,604
A dartboard would allocate research funding more rationally.

436
00:23:46,084 --> 00:23:50,364
A drunk person throwing darts at a list of diseases would produce a funding

437
00:23:50,364 --> 00:23:54,624
allocation that correlates more closely with actual disease burden than

438
00:23:54,624 --> 00:23:58,524
the National Institutes of Health, which employs twenty thousand people

439
00:23:58,524 --> 00:24:01,934
and has been doing this for fifty years.

440
00:24:02,104 --> 00:24:04,884
The dartboard doesn't even need to be in the building.

441
00:24:05,524 --> 00:24:07,124
Patients want medicine that works,

442
00:24:08,024 --> 00:24:12,924
access to experimental therapies, trials they can join, and a cure before

443
00:24:12,924 --> 00:24:13,584
they die.

444
00:24:14,204 --> 00:24:15,484
The N.I.H.

445
00:24:15,484 --> 00:24:17,124
funds molecular mechanisms,

446
00:24:17,804 --> 00:24:20,464
research empires, and institutional overhead.

447
00:24:21,324 --> 00:24:23,544
These two lists do not overlap.

448
00:24:23,764 --> 00:24:25,154
They don't even live in the same neighborhood.

449
00:24:25,964 --> 00:24:27,624
Patients don't control the money.

450
00:24:28,184 --> 00:24:29,024
Committees do.

451
00:24:29,404 --> 00:24:33,504
And committees optimize for the continued existence of committees.

452
00:24:33,944 --> 00:24:35,484
This is true of all committees,

453
00:24:36,144 --> 00:24:38,004
everywhere, since the invention of committees.

454
00:24:38,524 --> 00:24:42,584
Nobody has ever convened a committee that recommended fewer committees.

455
00:24:42,684 --> 00:24:47,404
On Wishonia, we have a word for an organism that exists solely to produce

456
00:24:47,404 --> 00:24:48,284
copies of itself.

457
00:24:48,924 --> 00:24:50,764
The word is "virus."

458
00:24:50,864 --> 00:24:53,184
You call them "advisory panels.".

459
00:24:53,384 --> 00:24:55,704
The Human Cost of Misallocation.

460
00:24:56,264 --> 00:25:00,664
When you allocate the vast majority of a forty-seven billion dollar annual

461
00:25:00,664 --> 00:25:05,584
budget into understanding disease instead of testing the safe,

462
00:25:06,264 --> 00:25:09,644
unpatentable treatments already gathering dust on the shelf,

463
00:25:10,284 --> 00:25:13,964
you get a very well-understood population of dead people.

464
00:25:14,584 --> 00:25:16,584
Cost Per Quality-Adjusted Life Year.

465
00:25:17,104 --> 00:25:20,424
A Quality-Adjusted Life Year is one year of healthy life.

466
00:25:21,264 --> 00:25:25,304
Lose a leg and live ten years, that's fewer than ten Q.A.L.Y.s.

467
00:25:26,044 --> 00:25:29,964
Die at forty instead of eighty, that's forty Q.A.L.Y.s lost.

468
00:25:30,564 --> 00:25:34,084
It's how you measure whether a medical system is keeping people alive and

469
00:25:34,084 --> 00:25:36,664
functional, or just keeping itself funded.

470
00:25:37,544 --> 00:25:41,944
The ADAPTABLE trial proved pragmatic trials cost forty-four point one times

471
00:25:41,944 --> 00:25:47,024
less per patient than traditional randomized controlled trials, or R.C.T.s

472
00:25:47,544 --> 00:25:51,004
(nine hundred and twenty-nine dollars versus forty-one thousand dollars).

473
00:25:51,764 --> 00:25:52,344
Same science.

474
00:25:53,024 --> 00:25:54,124
Fewer catered meetings.

475
00:25:54,944 --> 00:25:57,444
Forty-four point one times more patients enrolled.

476
00:25:58,004 --> 00:25:59,084
Fewer conference rooms rented.

477
00:26:00,184 --> 00:26:01,164
The Preventable Deaths.

478
00:26:02,504 --> 00:26:03,564
Conservative estimate:

479
00:26:03,644 --> 00:26:09,384
the N.I.H.'s misallocation costs approximately ten million Q.A.L.Y.s and

480
00:26:09,384 --> 00:26:12,064
seven hundred thousand preventable deaths every year.

481
00:26:12,684 --> 00:26:16,384
The upper bound is far worse (one hundred million Q.A.L.Y.s,

482
00:26:17,084 --> 00:26:18,184
seven million deaths),

483
00:26:18,924 --> 00:26:20,764
but even the floor is staggering.

484
00:26:21,384 --> 00:26:25,824
On Wishonia, if an institution's budget allocation was killing seven hundred

485
00:26:25,824 --> 00:26:30,084
thousand people a year, we would adjust the budget allocation.

486
00:26:30,864 --> 00:26:33,524
You adjusted the font on the annual report.

487
00:26:34,624 --> 00:26:38,484
Traditional clinical trials run at two point two seven percent the efficiency

488
00:26:38,484 --> 00:26:39,624
of pragmatic trials.

489
00:26:40,664 --> 00:26:44,804
And that's the ceiling, because it only accounts for the sliver of the N.I.H.

490
00:26:44,864 --> 00:26:46,644
budget that goes to trials at all.

491
00:26:47,384 --> 00:26:51,824
If your car ran at two point two seven percent efficiency, you would push

492
00:26:51,824 --> 00:26:53,084
it faster than it drives.

493
00:26:53,664 --> 00:26:56,614
If your heart pumped at two point two seven percent efficiency,

494
00:26:57,244 --> 00:26:59,044
you'd be dead before finishing this sentence.

495
00:26:59,684 --> 00:27:03,904
Your clinical trial system runs at two point two seven percent efficiency,

496
00:27:04,404 --> 00:27:05,324
and you gave it a raise.

497
00:27:05,904 --> 00:27:07,644
You gave it a raise and a new building.

498
00:27:08,304 --> 00:27:09,994
The building has a cafeteria.

499
00:27:10,984 --> 00:27:14,724
COVID is the most vivid example of what misallocation costs.

500
00:27:15,484 --> 00:27:18,544
So let me tell you what happened, and I will try to keep my composure,

501
00:27:19,404 --> 00:27:22,404
though I should warn you that I have been told I do not have composure.

502
00:27:23,784 --> 00:27:26,124
Your government knew this research was dangerous.

503
00:27:26,684 --> 00:27:31,364
In twenty fourteen, the Obama administration imposed a moratorium on gain-of-function

504
00:27:31,364 --> 00:27:31,944
research,

505
00:27:32,884 --> 00:27:36,604
specifically because engineering novel viruses posed pandemic risk.

506
00:27:37,184 --> 00:27:38,584
The government's own assessment:

507
00:27:39,284 --> 00:27:40,464
too dangerous to continue.

508
00:27:41,044 --> 00:27:43,984
In December twenty seventeen, the moratorium was lifted.

509
00:27:44,664 --> 00:27:46,484
There is evidence that N.I.H.

510
00:27:46,484 --> 00:27:50,804
officials may have effectively circumvented the pause the entire time regardless.

511
00:27:51,544 --> 00:27:56,684
